cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "MIGRA-IA: Intelligent agent for obsolescence diagnosis and migration of industrial automation systems"
abstract: >-
  The agent can be tried online, with nothing to install and no API key, at
  https://migra-ia.onrender.com — it is the interactive demo of the artifact
  itself; if the service is asleep, the first load may take about a minute.
  MIGRA-IA is an assisted conversational agent that guides technical staff
  step by step through the diagnosis of hardware obsolescence (PLCs, I/O
  modules, HMIs, industrial networks, drives) and through migration planning.
  It implements an adaptive questionnaire, a weighted obsolescence risk
  scoring engine (0–100), a traceable case file with an audit trail, mandatory
  safety rules and human validation. It includes a reproducible demonstration
  mode that runs without an API key (an independently evaluable artifact).
  Version 0.3.0 added the structured knowledge base MIGRA-IA-GUIA-001 (6
  methodological stages, 24 chapters, migration routes for 5 manufacturers, 20
  verification tests, 22 templates and 5 case studies), which the agent
  queries through a dedicated tool. Version 0.4.0 adds a platform catalog of
  30 manufacturers and 469 models, the migration procedure MIGRA-IA-PROC-050
  (50 numbered steps plus 7 preliminary ones, in 7 phases), the diagnostic
  questionnaire extended to 17 sections and an interactive mode that runs with
  no API key; it withdraws the guided demonstration mode, leaving the
  interface with two entry points, and incorporates a reproducible ordinal
  risk baseline with its frozen split. It also adds two routes that specialize
  the procedure according to the case: the manufacturer route when staying
  with the same brand, and the cross-manufacturer porting route when the
  target is from another brand and the source program is accessible and
  verified, which covers the internal memory inventory and the language
  census, the instruction equivalence table between both manufacturers, the
  triage of logic that can be carried over versus logic that must be
  rewritten, the address mapping from the original symbol table and the
  behavior comparison against the starting program, with the explicit limit
  that the agent does not publish equivalences it cannot cite. Version 0.5.0
  publishes the artifact in two languages — code, data, documentation,
  installation guides, interface and demonstration in Spanish and English,
  each document entirely in one language — and fixes a defect that interrupted
  the demonstration when the equipment's life-cycle status was declared
  unknown.
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-09-17"
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - obsolescence
  - hardware migration
  - knowledge base
  - industrial automation
  - PLC
  - AI agent
  - control systems
